{"id":"16.12.FlyingOrbit","contentHtml":"<p>This is my very <mark>first project in mobile development</mark>, which became my \"entry point\" into the industry. Despite the naivety of some decisions (for example, the entire UI was rendered in Blender), this project demonstrates my early ambitions and ability to independently master all aspects of development.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As a <strong>Solo Developer</strong>, I was responsible for <strong>100%</strong> of the implementation: from idea and 3D modeling to programming and game design.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>This was my <strong>first ambitious foray into mobile gamedev</strong>, which I initially planned to bring to release. The key task was to <strong>test myself: can I alone create a full-fledged mobile game.</strong></p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Engineering and Product Solution</h2>\n<p>Despite the lack of experience, I tried to implement all key elements of a full-fledged mobile game.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Core Mechanics:</strong> Developed simple <code>one-tap</code> gameplay where the player moves a ship between two \"rails\", dodging obstacles.</li>\n<li><strong>Thought-out Meta-Game:</strong> Designed a full game loop with a <strong>revive system</strong> and a mini-game in the form of a <strong>slot machine</strong> to win buffs.</li>\n<li><strong>Full Asset Creation Cycle:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>All 3D models (ship, planet, obstacles) and their textures were <strong>created and baked in Blender</strong>.</li>\n<li>The entire UI, despite the non-standard approach, was also modeled, rendered, and integrated.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Feature-Rich Prototype Created:</strong> The project was brought to the state of a <strong>fully playable prototype</strong> with a complex meta-game.</li>\n<li><strong>Gained Fundamental Experience:</strong> I <strong>mastered the entire pipeline</strong> of creating a 3D game in Unity in practice, from modeling to game design.</li>\n<li><strong>Starting Point for Growth:</strong> Although the game was not published, this ambitious first step <mark>formed that fundamental experience and knowledge</mark> that allowed making all subsequent releases successful.</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"Flying Orbit","date":"2016-12","type":"project","tagsArray":["Mobile","Arcade","Unity","C#","Blender"],"heroVideo":["u9Rxt5McsmY"],"shortDescription":"<p>My <strong>first ambitious foray into mobile gamedev</strong>: a solo prototype with a well-thought-out meta-game that became the foundation for future growth.</p>\n","role":"solo","storeLinks":["16.09.Realoft"],"projectIcon":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/card.video?v=1765111539601&webm=1&mp4=1","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/screenshots/1.webp","width":526,"height":936},{"src":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/screenshots/2.webp","width":526,"height":936},{"src":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/screenshots/3.webp","width":1920,"height":1080},{"src":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/screenshots/4.webp","width":526,"height":936},{"src":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/screenshots/5.webp","width":526,"height":936},{"src":"/images/projects/16.12.FlyingOrbit/screenshots/6.webp","width":526,"height":936}]}